    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ōvātus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		ovum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Eggshaped</i>, <i>ovate</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliis ovata species,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 21, 23, § 85</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 254 <i>med.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Having ovate spots</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapis Numidicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 1, 1, § 3</span></i>
			.</div>
